At first I intended for shaitan to go extinctionist, but after a
couple of experiments killing specific creatures I decided to call it
a day, and just ascend the poor chap.

Life did not start un eventful for shaitan: I started out with =oSI
and =oSD, an unremarkable wand and dito spellbook. So I decided to
take some risks and quaff form a few fountains, hoping to get See
Invis intrinsic, instead of via the ring. The very first:
"You unleash a water demon! -more-"
Whoops! At that point I was ready to start up a new character. But a
quick tab on the spacebar yielded the following:
"Grateful for her release, she grants you a wish! -more-"
Well, a SDSM please!

It got better, as some time afterwards I found a Magic lamp, a BoH,
GoP and some bags of tricks I'd have used to get magicbane. Frist I
wanted to clear out the mines though: in an effort to create some room
to pick up some gems I made a mistake: nice fireworks. And there went
my only bag.

Sokoban gave didn't yield another BoH, but instead the hardly useful
"oR. And because I didn't want to use my magic lamp there was only one
thing to do: go to the castle. I only stopped long enough at an altar
to get me Magicbane and Frostbrand. And Juiblex:-) whome I lured to
the bigroom level above me: he was forever getting in my way.

However, it obviously took a long time, because I forgot Magic Missile
in the proces. This made dealing with the Titan(tm) Medusa level
troublesome: the titan imediately casted create monster, so I had to
flee back upstairs, unable to use my /oDigging on the stairsquare.
Back upstairs I used my /oDigging to dig to back medusa: I ended up a
save distance from the titan. But not so far away from the water:
digging next to water was the reason I died the last time.

Okay, no problem, just move left and dig down there. I ended up in the
maze, near a minotaur who almost finished me off. But not quite:-) So
there I was, the caste, but no good attack spell. Wait a minute, I had
a magic marker, and a plain spell book:-) And after that, the castle
was easy again. The wand was 0:3, and my second wish was a BoH.
Finally:-)

Somewhere after that something funny happened: Some creature managed
to cast create high level monsters, including, much to my delight, 2
master mind flayers with a wand of death. Scary at first, but not
after the ray reflected from my armor.

Wand of Death in my hand it was time for the quest. Getting to the
Dark One was a breeze, killing him wasn't. I didn't remember quest
nemesi(?) teleport/heal, so I was forever waiting for him to show up
and hit me, never able to finish him off. That changed once I got
blinded by lightining and my telepathic powers forced me to notice the
Dark One at the upstairs.

Finally, the eye!

High Time to extinct all monsters. Les' start with ludios.
...
Then some random monsters with +oCM. boring.
Maybe rob a shop and kill some Kops. hmm _how many are there!_.
Gehenom then,... casting CM, but not creating very interesting
monsters.
Deeper down I had some fun with an Arch Lich (thanx, magicbane)
Back to random monsters. Didn't seem to go very fast.
Lets try and count some specific monsters:
So, I go back to the quest and start creating Wraiths, Xorn and most
of all: Vampire Bats. And I count'em Bats. 40. 60. 80. 100, must be
getting close. 120. Hmmz. 140? Argh!! Thats when I decided I didn't
wat to be an extinctionist after all:-)

The rest was a breeze: the most difficult thing was to decide what i'd
leave behind:-)
There was a bad virus on the loose, and rodney caught it. Often, and
fast. c!oGL got me out of the sanctum fast, and the misterious force
didn't do much harm either. I had 3 scrolls of Gold Detection, and
getting confused was easy too. Man, my pet angel even survived the
astral plane, it was that easy:-) This time I killed Famine (/oD) and
just like my other ascention (Slythe, Barb) it turned out I had
guessed correctly.

